            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "annual-maximum daily precipitation (Rx1day)",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Precipitation data in the Hadley Centre global land-based gridded climate extremes data set (HadEX2) is based on daily observations from about 11 600 precipitation stations gridded on a 2.54\u00b0 \u00d7 3.75\u00b0 grid from 1901 to 2010 (Donat et al., 2013). Here, gridded HadEX2 annual maximum 1-day precipitation data (Rx1day) are analyzed as the observation data set. The Rx1day extreme precipitation index is defined as the annual-maximum daily precipitation, in which the maximum 1-day precipitation amount is selected for each year.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
